e1000: use phylink for a CE4100 fixed link

The CE4100 GbE MAC's only interface is RGMII. Wired straight to a switch
port, it has no PHY on its MDIO bus: the PHY scan finds nothing and probe
fails.

If the device's OF node has a fixed-link, create a phylink instance from
the node and let it own the link. The MAC is forced to the speed, duplex
and pause phylink resolves, with transmit enabled on link up and disabled
on link down; a mutex orders this against MAC resets. Link state, ethtool
link and pause settings, autonegotiation restart and the MII ioctls go to
phylink, which is started and stopped with the interface, across suspend
and in PCI error recovery. e1000's own PHY accesses are refused. Only
rgmii phy modes are accepted, since the MAC's only interface is RGMII.

A failed PHY scan now returns -EIO itself, as phylink setup leaves err
cleared. Without a fixed-link, nothing changes.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
